STEP 1 — Navigation type test:
Click every nav link. Watch the browser URL bar.
Record what happens:

  A) URL changes to /work, /about, /contact AND page fully reloads/transitions
     → TYPE C: GSAP-driven virtual SPA (pages with animated transitions)
  B) URL does NOT change, or only the hash changes (#work, #about)
     → TYPE B: FULL-SCROLL SPA (everything in one document)
  C) URL changes AND you see distinct page loads with no shared persistent canvas
     → TYPE A: Standard MPA (separate Next.js pages per route)

STEP 2 — Document structure test:
  document.querySelectorAll('section, [data-section], [data-page], [data-panel], [data-slide]').length
  // Count > 3 inside ONE document = likely TYPE B

STEP 3 — Scroll library detection:
  console.log('FullPage.js:', !!window.fullpage_api)
  console.log('Locomotive:', !!window.locomotiveScroll)
  console.log('GSAP ST:', typeof gsap !== 'undefined' && !!gsap.ScrollTrigger)
  console.log('Lenis:', !!window.lenis)
  // GSAP ScrollTrigger pinning sections = TYPE B

STEP 4 — Virtual routing detection:
  window.__NEXT_DATA__  // present = Next.js
  window.history.state  // check pushState calls during navigation

DECLARE THE ARCHITECTURE TYPE BEFORE PROCEEDING:

  TYPE A — Standard MPA
  Each nav link = separate URL = separate Next.js page in /app directory.
  Build: normal pages, transitions between routes.

  TYPE B — Full-Scroll SPA ← THE MOST DANGEROUS ONE TO GET WRONG
  ALL content lives in ONE document. "Pages" are sections.
  Nav links scroll-to-section (or GSAP-pin-travel). URL may not change.
  Build rule: EVERYTHING in app/page.tsx. NO sub-pages for work/about/contact.
  Sections are React components stacked vertically, pinned via GSAP ScrollTrigger.
  Navigation uses scrollTo(sectionRef) — NEVER Next.js router.push().
  ⚠️ ACTIVE THEORY, AWWWARDS SITES, STUDIO PORTFOLIOS are often TYPE B.
  ⚠️ Building TYPE B as TYPE A = completely wrong experience = total failure.

  TYPE C — Virtual-Routing SPA (Barba.js / GSAP clip-path transitions)
  URL changes but NO full page reload. Transitions animate between views.
  Build rule: Next.js pages BUT every route change fires a clip-path or
  curtain transition. Page loader fires on every navigation. All pages share
  one persistent layout wrapper (cursor, audio, loader all persist).
  ⚠️ Building TYPE C without transitions = broken experience.

Write TYPE decision as: "ARCHITECTURE: TYPE [A/B/C] — reason: [evidence]"
